{% doc %}
  blocks/_testimonial-card.liquid — private to `sections/testimonials.liquid`.

  One review: who said it, what they bought, their stars, their words, and the
  product itself as a disc hanging off the bottom corner. Hovering the card
  raises a panel over the disc with the product's title, rating and price.

  ## Two boxes, because the design draws two

  The card is a ring and a filled panel with a gap between them:

      .testimonial-card          the ring — border, radius, and `--tc-ring-gap`
      .testimonial-card__frame   the panel the words sit in

  They are one element in most themes and two here because the ring changes on
  hover and the panel does not. Nesting them means the hover rule touches one
  property on one element rather than re-stating the panel's fill, radius and
  padding in a second state.

  The ring's settings are the theme's border group — style, four widths,
  opacity, colour, and a radius per breakpoint — resolved exactly as
  `blocks/_feature-card.liquid` resolves its own, including the `color-mix`
  fallback for a blank colour. A blank colour has no alpha channel to read until
  the scheme resolves in the browser, so the filters cannot fade it and
  `color-mix` does that job at paint time instead.

  ## The disc hangs outside the card, and that is deliberate

  It overhangs the ring's bottom edge by `--tc-thumb-overhang`, which is the
  section's setting rather than this block's — see the note beside it below.
  swiper.css gives the carousel element `overflow: hidden`, so the section pays
  for the overhang in padding under the track rather than by opting out of the
  clip: an element that is a scroll container on one axis cannot be `visible` on
  the other, and asking for that turns the track into something a trackpad can
  scroll vertically by accident.

  ## The panel is anchored to the card, the arrow to the disc

  The panel is a child of the frame and the disc is a sibling of it, and both
  are measured from `.testimonial-card` — the frame is never given `position`, so
  an absolute child of it resolves against the card instead. That is why the
  arrow's offset can subtract one inset from the other:

      arrow inset-end = thumb inset-end + thumb size / 2 − arrow width / 2 − panel inset

  The panel spans nearly the full width of the card while its arrow points at
  the disc in the corner, which is what the design does and what centring the
  panel on the disc could not do — a 250px panel centred on a disc 68px from
  the card's edge hangs 57px off the side of it.

  ## No product is a state, not an absence

  A card with nothing picked still draws the disc and still raises the panel.
  The disc is Shopify's product placeholder through `snippets/image.liquid` —
  same wrapper, same fade, same load behaviour as a real photograph — and the
  panel shows the four placeholder settings below it.

  That is the same call `blocks/_feature-card.liquid` makes about its hover
  picture, for the same reason: a card whose hover does nothing until a product
  is picked reads as a broken setting rather than an empty one, and the theme
  editor is where this section is judged.

  A picked product overrides all four. Its rating comes from
  `snippets/rating.liquid` — the reviews metafield every major app writes to —
  and falls back to the placeholder rating when the store has no review app, so
  the panel is never a title with a gap under it.

  ## Touch has no hover, so touch gets the panel

  Every hover rule in `base.css` sits inside `@media (hover: hover)` and is
  mirrored by an `@media (hover: none), (max-width: 749px)` block that makes the
  same state the resting one. The product's title and price are content, and
  content a phone can never reach is content that does not exist on a phone.

  `:focus-within` is paired with `:hover` throughout, so a keyboard reaching the
  product link gets the panel a pointer gets. The link only exists when a
  product is picked — a placeholder disc is not a destination.

  ## Three copies of every default

  The schema default, the `| default:` beside the setting that reads it, and the
  section preset. They have to agree: a card created from a preset that omits a
  setting has nothing stored, so it falls through to the Liquid fallback while
  the editor panel shows the schema's number.
  `blocks/_feature-card.liquid` documents the bug this caused there.
{% enddoc %}


{%- liquid
  assign s = block.settings

 
  assign border_line = s.border_style | default: 'solid'
  assign bw_top = 0
  assign bw_right = 0
  assign bw_bottom = 0
  assign bw_left = 0
  assign border_any = 0
  assign border_paint = ''

  if border_line != 'none'
    assign bw_top = s.border_width_top | default: 1 | plus: 0
    assign bw_right = s.border_width_right | default: 1 | plus: 0
    assign bw_bottom = s.border_width_bottom | default: 1 | plus: 0
    assign bw_left = s.border_width_left | default: 1 | plus: 0
    assign border_any = bw_top | plus: bw_right | plus: bw_bottom | plus: bw_left

    assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
    endif
  endif

 
  assign radius = s.border_radius | default: 20 | plus: 0
  assign radius_mobile = s.border_radius_mobile | default: radius | plus: 0
  assign ring_gap = s.ring_gap | default: 7 | plus: 0

  
  assign hover_line = s.hover_border_style | default: 'dashed'
  assign hover_paint = ''
  if s.hover_border_color != blank
    assign hover_percent = s.hover_border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    assign hover_alpha = hover_percent | divided_by: 100.0
    assign hover_paint = s.hover_border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', hover_alpha
  endif

  assign has_hover_border = false
  if hover_line != 'inherit' or hover_paint != ''
    assign has_hover_border = true
  endif

 
  assign frame_radius = s.frame_radius | default: 12 | plus: 0
  assign frame_radius_mobile = s.frame_radius_mobile | default: frame_radius | plus: 0

  assign frame_paint = ''
  if s.frame_background != blank
    assign frame_alpha = s.frame_background_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    assign frame_alpha = frame_alpha | divided_by: 100.0
    assign frame_paint = s.frame_background | color_modify: 'alpha', frame_alpha
  endif

  assign min_height = s.min_height | default: 350 | plus: 0

 
  assign star_size = s.star_size | default: 14 | plus: 0

 
  assign product = s.product
  assign has_product = false
  if product != blank
    assign has_product = true
  endif

  assign show_product = s.show_product
  if show_product == nil
    assign show_product = true
  endif

 
  assign info_title = s.placeholder_title | default: 'Morning Recovery'
  if has_product
    assign info_title = product.title
  endif

  assign product_rating = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value
  assign has_product_rating = false
  if has_product and product_rating != blank and product_rating.rating != blank
    assign has_product_rating = true
  endif

  assign info_rating = s.placeholder_rating | default: 5 | plus: 0
  assign info_reviews = s.placeholder_reviews | default: 889 | plus: 0

  assign show_info_rating = s.show_info_rating
  if show_info_rating == nil
    assign show_info_rating = true
  endif

  assign show_info_price = s.show_info_price
  if show_info_price == nil
    assign show_info_price = true
  endif

  comment
    The panel's id, so the disc's `aria-controls` has something to name. Block
    ids are unique per section, so two cards on one page cannot collide.
  endcomment
  assign panel_id = 'tc-panel-' | append: block.id

  comment
    ---- the classes ----
  endcomment
  assign card_classes = 'testimonial-card'
  if show_product
    assign card_classes = card_classes | append: ' testimonial-card--has-product'
  endif
  unless has_product
    assign card_classes = card_classes | append: ' testimonial-card--placeholder-product'
  endunless
  if has_hover_border
    assign card_classes = card_classes | append: ' testimonial-card--hover-border'
  endif

  comment
    `sizes` describes the widest the disc is ever painted. The section's slider
    tops out at 140px, so that is the hint: a wrong one here is the usual cause
    of a thumbnail arriving three sizes larger than the box it fills — on a row
    of five cards, five times over.
  endcomment
  assign thumb_sizes = '140px'
-%}

{%- capture card_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', block: s, declarations: true -%}
  --tc-ring-gap: {{ ring_gap }}px;
  --tc-frame-gap: {{ s.gap | default: 16 | plus: 0 }}px;
  --tc-radius: {{ radius }}px;
  --tc-radius-mobile: {{ radius_mobile }}px;
  --tc-frame-radius: {{ frame_radius }}px;
  --tc-frame-radius-mobile: {{ frame_radius_mobile }}px;
  --tc-transition: {{ s.hover_duration | default: 400 | plus: 0 }}ms;
  --tc-lift: {{ s.hover_lift | default: 0 | plus: 0 }}px;
  {%- if min_height > 0 -%}
    --tc-min-height: {{ min_height }}px;
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if border_any > 0 -%}
    --tc-border-width: {{ bw_top }}px {{ bw_right }}px {{ bw_bottom }}px {{ bw_left }}px;
    --tc-border-style: {{ border_line }};
    --tc-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if has_hover_border -%}
    {%- if hover_line != 'inherit' -%}
      --tc-hover-border-style: {{ hover_line }};
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if hover_paint != '' -%}
      --tc-hover-border-color: {{ hover_paint }};
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if frame_paint != '' -%}
    --tc-frame-background: {{ frame_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
<div
  class="{{ card_classes }}"
  style="{{ card_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- comment -%}
    `data-block-spacing` is on the frame and the `style` attribute is on the
    ring, which looks like a mistake and is not.

    The ring's own inset is `--tc-ring-gap` — the gap between the two boxes the
    design draws. The four padding sliders are the room inside the panel the
    words sit in, which is the frame. Custom properties inherit, so the ring can
    publish `--block-padding-*` and the frame can be the element that reads them.

    Putting the hook on the ring instead would give the ring 28px of padding and
    the frame none: one very fat ring around a panel with the text pressed
    against its edge.
  {%- endcomment -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    `<testimonial-product>` wraps the frame and the disc rather than sitting
    between them, because the panel it opens is inside the frame and the disc
    that opens it is not — this is the nearest element containing both.
    `display: contents` in `base.css` keeps it out of the card's layout, so the
    ring, the frame and the disc are positioned exactly as they were.

    It is rendered whether or not a product is picked: the placeholder panel is
    what a merchant is looking at while they configure the card, and a preview
    that only works once a product is chosen reads as broken rather than empty.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if show_product -%}<testimonial-product>{%- endif -%}

  <div class="testimonial-card__frame" data-block-spacing>
    {%- comment -%}
      The attribution sits above the quote rather than under it, which is where
      a `<figcaption>` would go. So it is a plain header row and the quote below
      it carries the `<cite>` through markup the HTML spec's own example for an
      attribution outside the quote uses.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="testimonial-card__head">
      <div class="testimonial-card__identity">
        {%- if s.author != blank -%}
          <cite class="testimonial-card__name">{{ s.author | escape }}</cite>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.role != blank -%}
          <span class="testimonial-card__role">{{ s.role | escape }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if s.show_verified and s.verified_label != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          A claim the merchant is making, so it is text rather than a glyph with
          a title attribute. The disc around the tick is decoration on top of a
          word that is already there.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="testimonial-card__verified">
          <span class="testimonial-card__verified-mark" aria-hidden="true">
            {% render 'icon', icon: 'check', size: 10 %}
          </span>
          {{ s.verified_label | escape }}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if s.rating > 0 -%}
      {% render 'rating-stars', rating: s.rating, size: star_size, class: 'testimonial-card__stars' %}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.quote != blank -%}
      <blockquote class="testimonial-card__quote">{{ s.quote }}</blockquote>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if show_product -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The product panel, and it lives inside the frame.

        On a pointer it is absolutely positioned and its containing block is
        `.testimonial-card` — the frame is deliberately never given `position`,
        so the panel and the disc are measured from the same box and the arrow's
        offset can subtract one inset from the other.

        On a touch screen `base.css` sets it back to `static`, and then it has to
        be a child of the frame or it would fall out of the panel it is drawn
        on. With the panel open on a phone, an absolutely positioned one covers
        the last two lines of every quote.

        It is not `aria-hidden`. A title and a price are content.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="testimonial-card__info" id="{{ panel_id }}" data-ref="panel">
        {%- comment -%}
          The title is the product's link, and the disc is not.

          A disc that navigates cannot also reveal — tap-to-reveal-then-tap-to-
          follow means the first tap on a product does nothing anyone asked for.
          So the picture opens the preview and the name goes to the product, at
          both breakpoints.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if has_product -%}
          <a class="testimonial-card__info-title" href="{{ product.url }}">{{ info_title }}</a>
        {%- else -%}
          <p class="testimonial-card__info-title">{{ info_title }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if show_info_rating -%}
          {%- if has_product_rating -%}
            {% render 'rating', product: product, class: 'testimonial-card__info-rating' %}
          {%- else -%}
            <div class="rating testimonial-card__info-rating">
              {% render 'rating-stars', rating: info_rating, size: 12, announce: false %}
              {%- if info_reviews > 0 -%}
                <span class="rating__count" aria-hidden="true">
                  ({{ 'products.product.rating_count' | t: count: info_reviews }})
                </span>
                <span class="visually-hidden">
                  {{- 'products.product.rating_html' | t: rating: info_rating, max: 5 }},
                  {{ 'products.product.rating_count' | t: count: info_reviews -}}
                </span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if show_info_price -%}
          {%- if has_product -%}
            {% render 'price', product: product, price_class: 'testimonial-card__info-price' %}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              The placeholder prices are typed, not money-filtered: they are two
              strings standing in for a product nobody has picked, and running a
              merchant's "$54.9" through `money` would need a number in the
              shop's base currency that they did not give.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="price testimonial-card__info-price">
              {%- if s.placeholder_compare_price != blank -%}
                <s class="price__compare">{{ s.placeholder_compare_price | escape }}</s>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if s.placeholder_price != blank -%}
                <span class="price__current">{{ s.placeholder_price | escape }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Only ever seen on a touch screen, where the panel opens on a tap
          rather than on a hover it can never receive. `base.css` hides it
          wherever the panel is a hover state, because a close button on
          something that closes itself when the pointer leaves is a control with
          nothing to do.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <button
          type="button"
          class="testimonial-card__info-close"
          data-ref="close"
          aria-label="{{ 'general.actions.close' | t }}"
        >
          {% render 'icon', icon: 'close', size: 12 %}
        </button>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- if show_product -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The disc is a sibling of the frame rather than a child of it. It hangs off
      the corner of the *card*, and a child of the frame would be measured from
      inside the frame's padding — so the four padding sliders would move the
      disc, which is not what they say they do.

      It is a button, not a link: it owns `aria-expanded` and points at the
      panel by id, so a keyboard user on a desktop gets the same explicit
      control a phone does rather than having to discover that focus alone
      reveals something.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button
      type="button"
      class="testimonial-card__thumb"
      data-ref="toggle"
      aria-expanded="false"
      aria-controls="{{ panel_id }}"
      aria-label="{{ info_title | escape }}"
    >
      {% render 'image',
         image: product.featured_image,
         alt: '',
         ratio: 'square',
         class: 'testimonial-card__thumb-image',
         placeholder: 'product-apparel-1',
         sizes: thumb_sizes %}
    </button>
  </testimonial-product>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.name",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "author",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial.settings.author.label",
      "default": "Jordan W."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "role",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.role.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.role.info",
      "default": "Morning Recovery"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "quote",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial.settings.quote.label",
      "default": "<p>Bite-sized insights that effortlessly fit into a busy morning routine. No fluff, just highly actionable habits that stick. A perfect daily reset button for mind and body.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "rating",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial.settings.rating.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.testimonial.settings.rating.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 5,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap",
      "label": "t:blocks.article_card.settings.gap.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.gap.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 48,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 16
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "star_size",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.star_size.label",
      "min": 10,
      "max": 24,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 14
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_verified",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.show_verified.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.show_verified.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "verified_label",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.verified_label.label",
      "default": "Verified",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.show_verified }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.headers.product"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.paragraphs.product"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_product",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.show_product.label",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "product",
      "id": "product",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.product.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.product.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_info_rating",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.show_info_rating.label",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.show_product }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_info_price",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.show_info_price.label",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.show_product }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.headers.placeholder"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.paragraphs.placeholder"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "placeholder_title",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.placeholder_title.label",
      "default": "Morning Recovery"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "placeholder_rating",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.placeholder_rating.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 5,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "number",
      "id": "placeholder_reviews",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.placeholder_reviews.label",
      "default": 889
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "placeholder_compare_price",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.placeholder_compare_price.label",
      "default": "$54.9"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "placeholder_price",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.placeholder_price.label",
      "default": "$44.9"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:shared.appearance.header"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "frame_background",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.frame_background.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.frame_background.info",
      "default": "#E5F1EE"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "frame_background_opacity",
      "label": "t:sections.feature_cards.settings.panel_background_opacity.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "frame_radius",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.frame_radius.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 12
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "frame_radius_mobile",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.frame_radius_mobile.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 12
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "min_height",
      "label": "t:blocks.feature_card.settings.min_height.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.settings.min_height.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 640,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 350
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.group.headers.borders"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:blocks.testimonial_card.paragraphs.borders"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "border_style",
      "label": "t:shared.border.style.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.options.none" },
        { "value": "solid", "label": "t:shared.options.solid" },
        { "value": "dashed", "label": "t:shared.options.dashed" },
        { "value": "dotted", "label": "t:shared.border.style.options__3.label" }
      ],
      "default": "solid"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_width_top",
      "label": "t:shared.border.sides.top.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 1,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_width_right",
      "label": "t:shared.border.sides.right.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 1,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_width_bottom",
      "label": "t:shared.border.sides.bottom.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
